# File manipulatorXZoneSet.template
#
# Several exclusion zone triggers can apply to the same axis motor
# limit and some could be active simultaneously.  Therefore this
# template combines them and chooses which one to enforce - the most
# restrictive one.  Can think of this template either as a set of
# exclusion zones on one motor limit or as a "setter" of the
# exclusion.  It also has to make sure that when an exclusion zone
# ceases to be active, the system either picks up the next most
# restrictive one or falls back to a valid state.  What happens then
# is the switch logic takes over, but that is handled in the
# manipulatorLimit template.  It might be true that an exclusion zone
# is active but the switch logic applies a more restrictive value.
# When the switch logic restriction goes away, that then has to fall
# through to the active exclusion.
#
# Currently we only have up to 1 or 2 triggers on each limit involved,
# but can handle up to 5 exclusions on the same limit (defined by upto 5
# instantiations of the manipulatorXZone template).
# This writes to the POSITIONS limit in the manipulatorLimit template
# and expects ptrs to records from the manipulatorXZone template.
